{"parentUuid": "7c3381d5-9603-4c63-b21c-4ffdcb6642e8", "isSidechain": true, "agentId": "ad5b9b485688e3b76", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "id": "msg_017jPv4cTj9rK8BjVSgKVFAR", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I now have all the information needed. The migration plan is clear, and the SQLite-specific code remaining in `app/db.py` and `app/config.py` is intentional \u2014 those are Tasks 3 and 2 respectively, which haven't been executed yet. Task 1 is scoped specifically to the dependency swap only.\n\n---\n\nAPPROVED\n\nThe Task 1 changes are correct and complete for their stated scope.\n\n**Dependency choice \u2014 `psycopg[binary]`:** Correct. The `[binary]` extra bundles `libpq`, eliminating the need for a system-level PostgreSQL client library install. This is the right choice for a Railway deployment where you control the runtime but want hermetic builds. The pure `psycopg` package (no extra) requires `libpq-dev` to be present on the host.\n\n**Version bound `<4`:** Correct. Major-version pinning is the standard practice for database drivers. psycopg has a history of breaking changes between major versions (psycopg2 \u2192 psycopg3 was not a drop-in replacement), so pinning `<4` is appropriate and intentional.\n\n**Remaining `aiosqlite` references:** All three hits are in docs files (`docs/health-reviews/` and `docs/superpowers/plans/`), which are historical records and the migration plan itself. These are not runtime references and require no cleanup.\n\n**SQLite-specific code in `app/db.py` and `app/config.py`:** The WAL pragma listener in `app/db.py` and the SQLite default URL in `app/config.py` are intentionally untouched \u2014 those are explicitly scoped to Tasks 2 and 3 in the migration plan. Task 1 is dependency-only by design.\n\n**`uv.lock` changes:** Clean. `aiosqlite` fully removed, `psycopg 3.3.3` + `psycopg-binary 3.3.3` added with correct platform wheels for both cp313 and cp314. The `tzdata` package was correctly pulled in as a conditional dependency (Windows-only per the lock file).\n\nNo issues found."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "cache_creation_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "cache_read_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "output_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]"}, "inference_geo": "", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "output_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "cache_read_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "cache_creation_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]", "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": "[SCRUBBED]"}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}}, "requestId": "req_011CaKfnUVkJ4pGKR5As9qA5", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "b0fa6716-aa69-42ef-8839-e40696a483d3", "timestamp": "2026-04-22T23:22:37.069Z", "advisorModel": "claude-opus-4-7", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "cli", "cwd": "/Users/test/Projects/studyengine/.worktrees/postgres-migration", "sessionId": "3f5802ab-0587-4c78-8a7e-80ca419e724f", "version": "2.1.117", "gitBranch": "test-branch"}
